MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience understanding management principles, practices, methods, techniques, and skill in integrating management services with the general management of an organization equivalent to the next lower grade level (GS-09) or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as:
1) Overseeing or administering administrative operations that ensure compliance with guidelines and requirements;
2) Providing administrative oversight and /or support to one or more of the various civilian and military personnel/ management programs;
3) Advising management on maintaining sound organization structures and improving management methods and procedures;
4) Collaborating with personnel specialists in finding solutions to arising issues that impact jobs and employees;
5) Resource planning, cost savings, budgeting, and personnel for the operation of a department. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
